    "done_when": "imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py Jt60saGeometryRegistry provides the five members §7 names, matching what imas_ambix/gs/machine_identity.py reads from nova.catalog.mast_geometry.MachineGeometryRegistry. registry_digest and dd_version are already present. configurations are keyed by physical digest, and each entry exposes physical_digest and authoring_gaps, the authoring gaps being that phase artifact's unresolved_gaps. select(shot) returns an object exposing .configuration and .evidence for the one phase range holding the shot, and raises KeyError outside both ranges. resolve_representation(digest) returns the configuration a phase's representation alias names, and raises KeyError for any other digest. Each phase has one alias: the SetupSignature digest MachineArtifactGeometryReader.read computes from that phase's artifact. Move that digest formula, today inline in MachineArtifactGeometryReader.read (round_geometry_hash over the probe r, z and angle, the flux-loop r and z, the filament r, z, width and height, and the limiter r and z), into one public function in imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py. read() calls it with its output unchanged, and the producer calls the same function over the same extracted parts. The aliases are part of the payload hashed into registry_digest, so the authored artifacts carry the moved digest. Also tighten _coil_drive_weight's agreement band from 1% relative to the catalogue's two-decimal rounding, an absolute band on the per-element weight just above 0.01 (two values each rounded to two decimals differ by at most 0.01, and 3.84 - 3.83 exceeds 0.01 in floating point), such as 0.011, with a test that a 0.02 disagreement on one CS1 connection is refused by coil name while the FPPC 3.83/3.84 pair is accepted. Add one public function in description_artifact.py that returns the registry built from the phase stores without materializing artifacts, for the selection node's default_registry to call. Tests in tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py: select(101173) returns the OP1 configuration with evidence observed; select(101174) returns OP2 with evidence inherited; select(99999) raises KeyError; each phase's configuration authoring_gaps equal its artifact's unresolved_gaps; the registry digest equals each artifact manifest's registry_digest; and, for each phase, reading the authored artifact with MachineArtifactGeometryReader gives a table whose signature digest resolve_representation maps to that phase's configuration. The existing tests in tests/gs/test_artifact_geometry.py and tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py keep passing. Write the landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-jt60sa-registry.html, quoting both aliases, the new registry digest and the new semantic identities. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the command, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py tests/gs/test_artifact_geometry.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
